  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nA weak short wave is currently moving through the area and will be \nfar south of the area by this evening. Some mid level clouds are \nexpected to form across our southwestern zones and along the KS/OK \nborder this afternoon. There may be an isolated thunderstorm that \nforms this afternoon in this area but quickly dissipate by early \nevening if they do form. Mostly clear skies are expected overnight \nand continue through the majority of the day tomorrow. A few \nthunderstorms may form across far western Kansas tomorrow afternoon \nbut are not expected to be severe. Winds are expected to be from an \neasterly direction through midnight then shift to the southeast \ntomorrow morning through tomorrow night. As for temperatures, highs \nthis afternoon are expected to range from the mid 90s along the I-70 \ncorridor to low 100s along the KS/OK border. We then dip into the \nupper 60s to low 70s tonight with 90s for highs tomorrow with around \n100 across far southwestern Kansas. Lows tomorrow night will once \nagain fall into the upper 60s to low 70s. \n\nThe upper level low will then be in place south of the area for the \nremainder of the forecast placing southwest Kansas under west to \nnorthwest flow aloft. A weak disturbance is expected to move over \nthis ridge Thursday night and bring an increased chance of \nthunderstorms Thursday afternoon into early Friday morning. The best \nchance of storms will be across the northern half of the CWA. The \nremainder of the forecast looks dry as high pressure becomes the \ndominate feature across the Central Plains. As for temperatures, \nhighs will generally reach into the 90s to low 100s with lows in the \nmid 60s to upper 70s.",
